summary: Get the list of available syscalls
description: |
    This pseudo-test retrieves a list of available
    syscall numbers by systematically trying every one
    from 0 to 600.

    Results location:
      output.txt
contact: Bilal Elmoussaoui <belmouss@redhat.com>
require:
  - gcc
component: kernel-automotive
test: bash runtest.sh
tier: 0
id: c4590b5d-6707-4030-9606-a63ae04b106c
adjust+:
  - enabled: false
    when: arch == x86_64
